Corrected message:

Offer to rasterize a live object before a paint tool draws on it

Any tool that writes to the current layer now checks the press point:
if it lands on a live shape/text object, the same rasterize prompt
Cut/Erase uses appears first. Accepting bakes just the object(s) under
the press as their own undo step; declining cancels the stroke.
Middle-button presses and mask painting are exempt.

Recolor also gets its own check that hit-tests the object's rendered
ink before prompting. A stroke that starts on bare ground never
prompts, even if it later crosses an object.
